.\" Hand-authored canonical man page for clearhead.
.\" src/bin/gen_man.rs produces a structural skeleton from clap definitions;
.\" this file is the authoritative reference and should not be overwritten.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el       .ds Aq '
.TH clearhead 1 "2026-05-17" "clearhead 0.2.1" "ClearHead Manual"
.\" ====================================================================
.SH NAME
.\" ====================================================================
clearhead \- plaintext action management: read, write, query, and archive .actions workspaces
.\" ====================================================================
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" ====================================================================
.B clearhead
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR]
.I verb
.I noun
[\fIoptions\fR]
[\fIarguments\fR]
.PP
.B clearhead
\fBread\fR \fBactions\fR|\fBplans\fR|\fBcharters\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBshow\fR \fBaction\fR|\fBplan\fR|\fBcharter\fR \fIquery\fR
.br
.B clearhead
\fBadd\fR \fBaction\fR|\fBplan\fR|\fBcharter\fR \fIname\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBupdate\fR \fBaction\fR|\fBplan\fR|\fBcharter\fR \fIquery\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBcomplete\fR \fBaction\fR \fIquery\fR
.br
.B clearhead
\fBcancel\fR \fBaction\fR \fIquery\fR
.br
.B clearhead
\fBdelete\fR \fBaction\fR|\fBplan\fR \fIquery\fR
.br
.B clearhead
\fBarchive\fR \fBactions\fR|\fBcharter\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBformat\fR|\fBlint\fR|\fBnormalize\fR \fBfile\fR [\fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBquery\fR \fBrun\fR|\fBnamed\fR|\fBlist\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B clearhead
\fBdebug\fR
.\" ====================================================================
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" ====================================================================
ClearHead is a plaintext-first personal action management system.
Work items (\fIactions\fR) live in \fB.actions\fR files that any text editor can read and write.
Recurring schedules live in \fB.ics\fR (vdir) files.
Completed history is accumulated in a single \fBarchive.ttl\fR Turtle file.
.PP
\fBclearhead\fR is the command-line interface and LSP server for the workspace.
It follows a \fIverb\-noun\fR command structure:
.EX
    clearhead read actions
    clearhead add action "Buy oat milk" \-\-charter inbox
    clearhead archive charter financial
.EE
.PP
All commands operate on the workspace rooted at \fBdata_dir\fR (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
Most commands accept \fB\-\-file\fR as an escape hatch to target an arbitrary file
outside the workspace.
.PP
Reference arguments (\fIquery\fR) accept any of:
full UUID, 8-character UUID prefix, alias (case-insensitive), or name
(case-insensitive, first match wins).
See
.B REFERENCE RESOLUTION
for details.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.\" ====================================================================
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Load configuration from \fIFILE\fR instead of the default
\fI~/.config/clearhead/config.json\fR.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Increase log verbosity.
Repeatable: \fB\-d\fR = DEBUG, \fB\-dd\fR = TRACE.
Diagnostic output is written to \fBstderr\fR.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help for the current command or subcommand.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH REFERENCE RESOLUTION
.\" ====================================================================
Wherever a \fIquery\fR argument is accepted, ClearHead resolves it in this order:
.RS 4
.TP 4
1.
Full UUID (\fI019eabcd\-1234\-7abc\-8def\-000000000000\fR)
.TP 4
2.
Short UUID prefix \(em first 8 characters (\fI019eabcd\fR)
.TP 4
3.
Alias \(em the \fB=alias\fR field on the item (case-insensitive)
.TP 4
4.
Name \(em the action or plan name (case-insensitive, first match)
.RE
.PP
Unresolved references produce a lint warning.
Ambiguous short UUIDs (more than one match) produce lint warning \fBW011\fR.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.\" ====================================================================
.SS "read \(em list items"
.PP
.B clearhead read actions
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR]
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIref\fR]
[\fB\-\-context\fR \fItag\fR]...
[\fB\-\-open\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
List actions across the workspace (default) or scoped to a charter, plan,
context, or explicit file.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format: \fBtable\fR (default), \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR
Scope to one charter (name, alias, or UUID).
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fIref\fR
Filter to actions belonging to a specific plan.
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR \fItag\fR
Filter by context tag.
Repeatable.
Includes tag hierarchy ancestors.
.TP
\fB\-\-open\-only\fR
Exclude Completed and Cancelled actions.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Read from an explicit \fB.actions\fR file instead of the workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns\fR \fIcols\fR
Show only these columns (comma-separated: \fBname,state,priority\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-hide\-columns\fR \fIcols\fR
Hide these columns.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-columns\fR
List all available column names and exit.
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead read plans
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR]
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-stdio\fR]
.PP
List recurring schedule Plans (\fB.ics\fR VTODOs) across the workspace or scoped to a charter.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR
Scope to one charter's \fBplans/\fR directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-recursive\fR
Include sub-charter plans (requires \fB\-\-charter\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-stdio\fR
Read from standard input.
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead read charters
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR]
[\fB\-\-explicit\-only\fR]
.PP
List all discovered charters in the workspace, shown hierarchically.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-explicit\-only\fR
Show only charters backed by a \fB.md\fR or \fBREADME.md\fR file;
omit charters inferred from \fB.actions\fR file stems alone.
.RE
.PP
Graph queries are provided by the separate \fBclearhead-graphd\fR tool. For
example, run \fBclearhead-graphd query index agenda\fR for the daily agenda.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "show \(em inspect a single item"
.PP
.B clearhead show action
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
Print all fields of a single action identified by \fIquery\fR.
Searches open actions first, then \fB.completed.actions\fR.
.PP
.B clearhead show plan
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-F\fR \fIfmt\fR]
.PP
Print all fields of a single recurring VTODO Plan.
.PP
.B clearhead show charter
\fIquery\fR
.PP
Print metadata for a charter (title, alias, state, description).
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "add \(em create new items"
.PP
.B clearhead add action
\fIname\fR
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR | \fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-parent\fR \fIref\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIstate\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR \fIalias\fR]
[\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Add a new action to a charter's \fB.actions\fR file.
A UUIDv7 and creation timestamp are assigned automatically.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR
Route to the named charter's \fB.actions\fR file.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-file\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Write to an explicit \fB.actions\fR file.
.TP
\fB\-\-parent\fR \fIref\fR
Attach as a child of the given action (UUID or short UUID).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIn\fR
Priority 1\(en9 (1 = highest urgency).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-state\fR \fIstate\fR
Initial state: \fBnot\-started\fR (default), \fBin\-progress\fR, \fBblocked\fR.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-alias\fR \fIalias\fR
Stable short name for cross-references.
.TP
\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR
Do date/time in RFC 3339 format (e.g. \fI2026-06-01T09:00:00-07:00\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would be added without writing.
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead add plan
\fIname\fR
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR | \fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR]
[\fB\-\-rrule\fR \fIRRULE\fR]
[\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Add a new schedule plan as a single-event \fB.ics\fR file inside the charter's
\fBplans/\fR directory.
Plans describe \fIwhen\fR actions should be generated; they do not hold action state.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR
DTSTART for the VTODO (RFC 3339).
.TP
\fB\-\-rrule\fR \fIRRULE\fR
RFC 5545 recurrence rule, e.g. \fIFREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR
Template to bind via VTODO DESCRIPTION (stem of a \fBtemplates/\fR file).
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead add charter
\fItitle\fR
[\fB\-a\fR \fIalias\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIparent\fR]
[\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Create a new charter.
A flat charter produces \fI<alias>.actions\fR and \fI<alias>.md\fR.
If a parent is given and the parent uses directory form, a subdirectory is
created instead.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-alias\fR \fIalias\fR
Short name; used as the file/directory stem.
Defaults to a slugified form of \fItitle\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-parent\fR \fIref\fR
Parent charter reference; places the new charter as a sub-charter.
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR
Scaffold the new charter's \fB.actions\fR file from a template.
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "update \(em modify existing items"
.PP
.B clearhead update action
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIstate\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR \fIalias\fR]
[\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Update one or more fields on an existing action.
Only supplied flags are changed; all other fields are left intact.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-state\fR \fIstate\fR
New state: \fBnot\-started\fR, \fBin\-progress\fR, \fBblocked\fR,
\fBcompleted\fR, \fBcancelled\fR.
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead update plan
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-scheduled\-at\fR \fIdatetime\fR]
[\fB\-\-rrule\fR \fIRRULE\fR]
[\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Update fields on a recurring VTODO Plan.
.PP
.B clearhead update charter
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-s\fR \fIstate\fR]
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fItitle\fR]
[\fB\-\-alias\fR \fIalias\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Update a charter's metadata.
Setting \fB\-\-state closed\fR is the prerequisite for \fBarchive charter\fR.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-state\fR \fIstate\fR
Lifecycle state: \fBnew\fR, \fBactive\fR, \fBblocked\fR, \fBclosed\fR.
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "complete \(em mark an action done"
.PP
.B clearhead complete action
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Set the action's state to \fBCompleted\fR and append a \fB%\fR completion
timestamp.
The action is moved from \fB<charter>.actions\fR to
\fB<charter>.completed.actions\fR.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "cancel \(em mark an action cancelled"
.PP
.B clearhead cancel action
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Set the action's state to \fBCancelled\fR without deleting it.
The action is moved to \fB<charter>.completed.actions\fR.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "delete \(em remove an item"
.PP
.B clearhead delete action
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Permanently remove an action from the workspace.
Searches open actions first, then \fB.completed.actions\fR.
This is destructive; prefer \fBcancel\fR for audit-trail preservation.
.PP
.B clearhead delete plan
\fIquery\fR
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Remove a recurring VTODO Plan resource from the workspace.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "archive \(em move completed work out of active files"
.PP
.B clearhead archive actions
[\fIscope\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Sweep Completed and Cancelled actions from \fB<charter>.actions\fR into
\fB<charter>.completed.actions\fR across the whole workspace (default) or
within a scoped charter path.
This is a routine housekeeping step; it does not delete history.
.RS 4
.TP
\fIscope\fR
Optional charter domain path: \fIhealth\fR, \fIwork/clearhead\fR, etc.
Workspace-wide if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Target a specific \fB.actions\fR file directly (out-of-workspace use).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print action counts without writing.
.RE
.PP
.B clearhead archive charter
[\fIquery\fR | \fB\-\-closed\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Sweep a fully closed charter's artifacts into \fBarchive.ttl\fR and remove
its source files.
The charter must carry \fBstate: Closed\fR in its frontmatter (set with
\fBupdate charter \-\-state closed\fR).
.RS 4
.TP
\fIquery\fR
Charter to archive (name, alias, or UUID prefix).
.TP
\fB\-\-closed\fR
Archive all charters whose frontmatter carries \fBstate: Closed\fR in one
pass.
Mutually exclusive with \fIquery\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Archive even if open actions remain in the primary \fB.actions\fR file
(they are cancelled and swept).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would be archived without writing or deleting.
.RE
.PP
What \fBarchive charter\fR does:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 4
Completed actions from \fB<charter>.completed.actions\fR \(-> \fBarchive.ttl\fR
.IP \(bu 4
Plan VTODOs from \fBplans/<charter>/\fR \(-> \fBarchive.ttl\fR
.IP \(bu 4
Charter metadata itself \(-> \fBarchive.ttl\fR
.IP \(bu 4
Empty source files and directories are removed
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "format \(em normalise file layout"
.PP
.B clearhead format file
[\fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-w\fR]
[\fB\-\-style\fR \fIstyle\fR]
[\fB\-\-indent\-style\fR \fIindent\fR]
[\fB\-\-indent\-width\fR \fIn\fR]
.PP
Format a \fB.actions\fR file: sort fields into canonical order, normalise
spacing, and reindent children.
If \fIpath\fR is omitted, reads from \fBstdin\fR and writes to \fBstdout\fR.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
Overwrite the input file with the formatted output.
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR \fIstyle\fR
\fBcompact\fR (default): all metadata on one line.
\fBlist\fR: each metadata field on its own indented line.
.TP
\fB\-\-indent\-style\fR \fIindent\fR
\fBspaces\fR (default) or \fBtabs\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-indent\-width\fR \fIn\fR
Number of spaces (or tabs) for child indentation (default 4).
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "lint \(em validate a file"
.PP
.B clearhead lint file
[\fIpath\fR]
.PP
Check a \fB.actions\fR file for errors and convention violations.
Reads from \fBstdin\fR if \fIpath\fR is omitted.
Exits non-zero if any errors are found.
.PP
Diagnostic codes are prefixed \fBE\fR (error), \fBI\fR (info/warning), or \fBW\fR (warning).
See
.B DIAGNOSTICS
for the full list.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "normalize \(em assign missing UUIDs"
.PP
.B clearhead normalize file
[\fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-w\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-format\fR]
.PP
Assign UUIDv7 identifiers to any action that lacks a \fB#\fR field, then
format the result.
Idempotent: existing UUIDs are never changed.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
Overwrite the input file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-format\fR
Skip the formatting step after assigning UUIDs.
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "patch \(em merge two versions of a file"
.PP
.B clearhead patch file
\fB\-p\fR \fIprimary\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsecondary\fR
[\fB\-w\fR]
.PP
Apply changes from \fIsecondary\fR onto \fIprimary\fR using UUID-keyed
three-way merge semantics.
Useful for reconciling edits made in two editors simultaneously.
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-primary\fR \fIpath\fR
Source of truth file.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-secondary\fR \fIpath\fR
File containing updates to apply.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
Overwrite \fIprimary\fR with the merged result.
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "expand \(em materialise scheduled instances"
.PP
.B clearhead expand actions
[\fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Expand recurring Plans (\fB.ics\fR VTODOs) into concrete action instances in
the corresponding \fB.actions\fR files.
Generates up to \fBexpansion_primary_instances\fR actions into the primary
\fB.actions\fR file and additional instances into \fB.upcoming.actions\fR.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "apply \(em instantiate a template"
.PP
.B clearhead apply template
\fIname\fR
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR | \fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Append the actions defined in \fIname\fR.actions (from the workspace
\fBtemplates/\fR directory) into a charter's \fB.actions\fR file.
New UUIDs are assigned to all appended actions.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "export \(em convert to external formats"
.PP
.B clearhead export plans
[\fIreference\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-open\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
.PP
Export Actions as standalone iCalendar VTODO components. Unscheduled and
due-only Actions are representable; \fB\-\-open\-only\fR excludes terminal states.
.RS 4
.TP
\fIreference\fR
Charter, plan, or action alias/UUID to scope the export.
Exports the entire workspace if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
Output file.
Writes to \fBstdout\fR if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-open\-only\fR
Exclude Completed and Cancelled items.
.TP
\fB\-\-recursive\fR
Include sub-charter plans (requires \fIreference\fR).
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "import \(em ingest external formats"
.PP
.B clearhead import plans
\fIsource\fR
[\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-overwrite\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Import recurring VTODO schedules and write individual VTODO+RRULE resources
inside the target charter's \fBplans/\fR vdir.
.RS 4
.TP
\fIsource\fR
\fB.ics\fR file to import (e.g. a Google Calendar export).
.TP
\fB\-\-charter\fR \fIname\fR
Target charter.
Defaults to the source filename stem.
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Replace existing \fI<UID>.ics\fR files when a UID collision occurs.
.RE
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "graph queries"
.PP
SPARQL execution, saved query families, validation, and query output formats
belong to the independently installed \fBclearhead-graphd\fR tool. The CLI does
not proxy that interface. See \fBclearhead-graphd --help\fR.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "sync \(em synchronise with external systems"
.PP
.B clearhead sync events
[\fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.PP
Backfill action-created telemetry records for existing actions.
.PP
.B clearhead sync calendar
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-conflict\fR \fIaction|calendar\fR]
.PP
Synchronize standalone Action VTODOs through the configured plans vdir.
Calendar-created VTODOs become Actions; missing projections are recreated.
No CalDAV server or transport implementation is assumed.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "start \(em launch services"
.PP
.B clearhead start lsp
.PP
Start the Language Server Protocol server on \fBstdin\fR/\fBstdout\fR using
the LSP 3.17 JSON-RPC protocol.
Editors attach to it automatically; invoke directly only for debugging.
See
.B LSP
below.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SS "debug \(em inspect resolved configuration"
.PP
.B clearhead debug
.PP
Print the fully resolved configuration (data_dir, config_dir, binary path,
workspace roots discovered) and any workspace-level diagnostics.
Useful for verifying setup after installation.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH "THE .ACTIONS FORMAT"
.\" ====================================================================
A \fB.actions\fR file is a list of actions, one per line (plus optional
continuation lines for descriptions).
Every action starts with a \fIstate marker\fR.
.PP
.B States
.RS 4
.TP 10
\fB[ ]\fR
Not started
.TP 10
\fB[-]\fR
In progress
.TP 10
\fB[=]\fR
Blocked / awaiting
.TP 10
\fB[x]\fR
Completed
.TP 10
\fB[_]\fR
Cancelled
.RE
.PP
.B Fields
(all optional except state and name; canonical order shown)
.RS 4
.TP
\fB=\fR\fIalias\fR
Stable short name for cross-references.
.TP
\fB$ ... $\fR
Description block.
Opens and closes with \fB$\fR; may span multiple lines.
.TP
\fB~\fR
Sequential children marker: direct children must be completed in order.
.TP
\fB!\fR\fIn\fR
Priority (1\(en9; 1 = highest urgency).
.TP
\fB*\fR\fIref\fR
Objective or parent reference.
Supports path notation: \fB*work/clearhead/docs\fR.
.TP
\fB+\fR\fItag\fR[,\fItag\fR]...
Context tags.
.TP
\fB@\fR\fIdatetime\fR
Do date/time \(em when you intend to work on this.
.TP
\fB:\fR\fIdatetime\fR
Due date/time \(em hard deadline.
.TP
\fB^\fR\fIdatetime\fR
Created timestamp (assigned automatically on first normalize/save).
.TP
\fB%\fR\fIdatetime\fR
Completed timestamp (assigned automatically on \fBcomplete\fR).
.TP
\fB#\fR\fIuuid\fR
Stable identifier (UUIDv7; assigned automatically on normalize/save).
.TP
\fB<\fR\fIref\fR
Predecessor: must be closed before this action is dependency-clean.
.RE
.PP
.B Children
.PP
Actions nest with \fB>\fR depth markers.
One \fB>\fR = depth 1, \fB>>\fR = depth 2, and so on.
Leading whitespace is cosmetic and ignored by the parser.
.EX
    [ ] Plan offsite
    > [ ] Book venue @2026-07-01
    > [ ] Arrange travel ~
    >> [ ] Book flights
    >> [ ] Book hotels
    > [ ] Send invites
.EE
.PP
.B Dates
.PP
ISO 8601 date/time forms are accepted.
Time zones are optional; local time is assumed when omitted.
.EX
    @2026-05-17
    @2026-05-17T14:30
    @2026-05-17T14:30:00-07:00
.EE
.PP
.B Full example
.EX
    [-] Ship v1.0 =ship-v1 !1 *clearhead @2026-06-01T09:00
        $ Final release checklist. Sequential. $
        ~ +work ^2026-05-01T10:00 #019eabcd-1234-7000-8000-000000000001
    > [ ] Run tests !2 +ci
    > [ ] Build binary !1 =build-binary
    > [ ] Tag release !1 < build-binary
    > [ ] Publish !1
    > [ ] Announce !3
.EE
.\" ====================================================================
.SH WORKSPACE
.\" ====================================================================
A ClearHead workspace is a directory that contains action files, schedule
plans, objectives, and configuration.
There are two workspace scopes:
.TP
.B Global (user) workspace
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/clearhead/\fR (default: \fI~/.local/share/clearhead/\fR)
.TP
.B Project workspace
The nearest ancestor directory containing a \fB.clearhead/\fR subdirectory.
.PP
.B Directory layout
.EX
    <workspace>/
    ├── archive.ttl              # closed history (Turtle RDF)
    ├── charters/
    │   ├── inbox.actions        # default capture zone
    │   ├── <charter>.actions    # flat charter actions
    │   ├── <charter>.completed.actions
    │   ├── <charter>.upcoming.actions
    │   ├── <charter>.md         # charter metadata / description
    │   └── <charter>/           # directory-form charter
    │       ├── README.md
    │       ├── next.actions
    │       └── <sub>.actions
    ├── objectives/
    │   └── <alias>.md
    ├── plans/
    │   └── <charter>/
    │       └── <resource>.ics   # one primary component per vdir resource
    └── templates/
        └── <name>.actions
.EE
.PP
For a project workspace, all of the above lives inside \fB.clearhead/\fR at
the project root.
The root charter's actions are at \fB.clearhead/charters/next.actions\fR.
.PP
\fBarchive.ttl\fR is the only file written by \fBarchive charter\fR.
It accumulates all closed history and is never deleted.
Query workspace graph data directly with \fBclearhead-graphd\fR using SPARQL.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH WORKFLOW
.\" ====================================================================
A typical daily workflow:
.PP
.B 1. Capture
.PP
Dump everything into the inbox without worrying about organisation:
.EX
    clearhead add action "Reply to Alice" --charter inbox +work
    clearhead add action "Pick up prescription" +health \\
        --scheduled-at "2026-05-18T10:00:00"
.EE
.PP
Or open the inbox in your editor (\fB:ClearheadInbox\fR in Neovim) and type
actions directly.
.PP
.B 2. Triage
.PP
Move actions to their home charters, set priorities, add dates:
.EX
    clearhead update action "Reply to Alice" --charter work -p 2
    clearhead update action "Pick up prescription" -p 1
.EE
.PP
.B 3. Act
.PP
Mark items in progress, then complete them:
.EX
    clearhead update action buy-oat-milk --state in-progress
    clearhead complete action buy-oat-milk
.EE
.PP
.B 4. Housekeep
.PP
Archive completed actions out of active files periodically:
.EX
    clearhead archive actions              # workspace-wide
    clearhead archive actions health       # one charter
.EE
.PP
.B 5. Review and close
.PP
When a charter's work is done, close and archive it:
.EX
    clearhead update charter financial --state closed
    clearhead archive charter financial --dry-run   # preview
    clearhead archive charter financial             # for real
.EE
.\" ====================================================================
.SH "LSP"
.\" ====================================================================
ClearHead includes a built-in Language Server Protocol (LSP 3.17) server.
Start it with:
.EX
    clearhead start lsp
.EE
Editors attach over \fBstdin\fR/\fBstdout\fR.
The official Neovim plugin (\fBclearhead.nvim\fR) configures this automatically
when \fBnvim_lsp_enable = true\fR.
.PP
Capabilities provided:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 4
Completions for \fB@\fR, \fB%\fR, \fB^\fR date fields ("now", "today", "tomorrow")
.IP \(bu 4
Code actions: assign UUID, set completion date, backfill creation date
.IP \(bu 4
Semantic tokens: state, name, priority, dates, UUID, tags, references
.IP \(bu 4
Inlay hints: due-date countdown, completion age
.IP \(bu 4
Go to definition / find references for objectives and context tags
.IP \(bu 4
Document formatting (delegates to \fBformat file\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
Diagnostics: all lint rules evaluated on every change
.IP \(bu 4
Workspace command \fBclearhead/archive\fR: returns a WorkspaceEdit
.RE
.\" ====================================================================
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.\" ====================================================================
\fBclearhead lint\fR and the LSP server both emit diagnostics using these codes.
Errors (\fBE\fR) block normalization; infos (\fBI\fR) and warnings (\fBW\fR)
are advisory.
.PP
.B Errors
.RS 4
.TP
\fBE001\fR
Duration field present without a do date (\fB@\fR).
.TP
\fBE003\fR
Empty context tag (\fB+\fR with no name).
.TP
\fBE004\fR
Orphaned child marker: \fB>\fR with no parent action above it.
.TP
\fBE005\fR
Skipped hierarchy level (e.g. root action followed directly by depth 2).
.TP
\fBE006\fR
Malformed UUID \(em not a valid UUID string.
.RE
.PP
.B Informational
.RS 4
.TP
\fBI001\fR
Completed action missing a completion date (\fB%\fR).
.TP
\fBI002\fR
Completion date present on a non-completed action.
.TP
\fBI003\fR
Invalid priority value (must be 1\(en9).
.TP
\fBI004\fR
Duplicate UUID in the workspace.
.TP
\fBI006\fR
Fields out of canonical order.
.TP
\fBI007\fR
High-priority action (1 or 2) without a do date.
.TP
\fBI008\fR
Blocked action (\fB[=]\fR) without a description explaining the blocker.
.TP
\fBI009\fR
Child action has higher priority than its parent.
.TP
\fBI010\fR
Duration exceeds a reasonable threshold.
.TP
\fBI011\fR
Do date is in the past.
.TP
\fBI012\fR
Alias does not match the required slug format.
.TP
\fBI013\fR
Redundant tag (already present via tag hierarchy ancestor).
.TP
\fBI014\fR
Objective path depth exceeds configured maximum.
.TP
\fBI015\fR
Empty alias (\fB=\fR with no name).
.RE
.PP
.B Warnings
.RS 4
.TP
\fBW001\fR
Hierarchy depth exceeded (more than the configured max nesting level).
.TP
\fBW002\fR
Completed parent action with one or more uncompleted children.
.TP
\fBW003\fR
All children are completed but the parent action is not.
.TP
\fBW004\fR
Action missing a creation date (\fB^\fR).
.TP
\fBW005\fR
Creation date is in the future.
.TP
\fBW006\fR
Completion timestamp is earlier than creation timestamp.
.TP
\fBW010\fR
Duplicate alias in the workspace.
.TP
\fBW011\fR
Ambiguous short UUID: more than one action matches the 8-char prefix.
.TP
\fBW012\fR
Sequential marker (\fB~\fR) on an action with no children.
.TP
\fBW013\fR
Incomplete UUID: a \fB#\fR id that is a well-formed prefix of a full UUID but stops short \(em a uuid still being typed. Contrast \fBE006\fR, a genuinely malformed id.
.RE
.\" ====================================================================
.SH CONFIGURATION
.\" ====================================================================
Configuration is resolved in this order (later sources win):
.RS 4
.IP "1." 4
Built-in defaults
.IP "2." 4
\fI~/.config/clearhead/config.json\fR
.IP "3." 4
Environment variables (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT )
.IP "4." 4
Command-line flags
.RE
.PP
\fBconfig.json\fR example:
.EX
    {
      "data_dir": "~/.local/share/clearhead",
      "default_file": "inbox.actions",
      "cli_format": "table",
      "expansion_primary_instances": 3
    }
.EE
.\" ====================================================================
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.\" ====================================================================
.TP
\fBCLEARHEAD_DATA_DIR\fR
Override the workspace data directory.
.TP
\fBCLEARHEAD_CONFIG_DIR\fR
Override the configuration directory.
.TP
\fBCLEARHEAD_DEFAULT_FILE\fR
Override the default actions file stem (default: \fBinbox.actions\fR).
.TP
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR
Base for \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/clearhead\fR (default: \fI~/.local/share\fR).
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Base for \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clearhead\fR (default: \fI~/.config\fR).
.\" ====================================================================
.SH FILES
.\" ====================================================================
.TP
\fI~/.config/clearhead/config.json\fR
User configuration file.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/clearhead/\fR
Default global workspace data directory.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/clearhead/charters/inbox.actions\fR
Default inbox (uncategorised captures).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/clearhead/archive.ttl\fR
Permanent closed history in Turtle RDF format.
.TP
\fI<project>/.clearhead/\fR
Project-local workspace root.
.TP
\fI~/.clearhead/queries/\fR
User-level named SPARQL queries.
.TP
\fI<project>/.clearhead/queries/\fR
Project-level named SPARQL queries.
.\" ====================================================================
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" ====================================================================
.B Daily capture
.EX
    # Open inbox in editor (clearhead.nvim)
    # Or add from the shell:
    clearhead add action "Review PR #412" --charter work +review -p 2
    clearhead add action "Call dentist" +health @2026-05-18T10:00
.EE
.PP
.B List open actions for a charter
.EX
    clearhead read actions --charter work --open-only
    clearhead read actions --charter work --format json | jq '.[] | .name'
.EE
.PP
.B Complete and archive
.EX
    clearhead complete action "Review PR #412"
    clearhead archive actions work
.EE
.PP
.B Close a charter
.EX
    clearhead update charter work --state closed
    clearhead archive charter work --dry-run
    clearhead archive charter work
.EE
.PP
.B Add a recurring weekly plan
.EX
    clearhead add plan "Weekly review" \\
        --charter inbox \\
        --scheduled-at "2026-05-19T09:00:00-07:00" \\
        --rrule "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO" \\
        --template weekly-review
    clearhead expand actions
.EE
.PP
.B Query blocked actions with SPARQL
.EX
    clearhead-graphd query raw --where '
        ?action a actions:Action ;
                cco:ont00001868 actions:Blocked ;
                rdfs:label ?name .
    '
.EE
.PP
.B Lint before committing
.EX
    clearhead lint file .clearhead/charters/next.actions
    echo $?   # 0 = clean, 1 = errors found
.EE
.PP
.B Export a charter's schedule to Apple Calendar
.EX
    clearhead export plans work -o work.ics
    open work.ics   # macOS: imports into Calendar.app
.EE
